{
  "id": "sat-linfun",
  "chapterNumber": "2",
  "title": {
    "en": "Linear Functions &amp; Inequalities",
    "ar": null
  },
  "chapterTag": {
    "variant": "category",
    "className": "sat-domain-tag",
    "emoji": "📌",
    "categoryPrefix": "Domain:",
    "category": "Algebra",
    "topics": [
      "Linear functions",
      "Linear inequalities in one or two variables"
    ]
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A linear function models a constant rate of change; an inequality describes a region rather than a single line.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Functions &amp; inequalities",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "For \\( f(x)=mx+b \\), \\( m \\) is the rate and \\( b \\) the starting value. Parallel lines share a slope; perpendicular slopes multiply to \\( -1 \\). An inequality's boundary line is dashed for \\( &lt; \\) or \\( &gt; \\), solid for \\( \\le \\) or \\( \\ge \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Adjust the slope \\( m \\) and intercept \\( b \\) of \\( y=mx+b \\). The amber dots mark the intercepts the SAT most often asks for.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Slope &amp; intercepts",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "satLineCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "The line y equals m x plus b with adjustable slope and intercept",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "satLineDataBtn",
          "panelId": "satLineDataPanel",
          "descId": "satLineDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "satLineDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points along the current line",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "y",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "satM",
            "label": {
              "en": "Slope <b>m =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -3,
            "max": 3,
            "value": 1,
            "step": 0.5,
            "valueDisplayId": "satMV",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Slope m",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "satB",
            "label": {
              "en": "Intercept <b>b =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -5,
            "max": 5,
            "value": 1,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "satBV",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Intercept b",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "satLineSlope",
            "label": {
              "en": "slope",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "—"
          },
          {
            "id": "satLineYint",
            "label": {
              "en": "y-intercept",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "—"
          },
          {
            "id": "satLineXint",
            "label": {
              "en": "x-intercept",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "—"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "The y-intercept is \\( (0,b) \\); the x-intercept solves \\( mx+b=0 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Function",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f(x)=mx+b \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "x-intercept",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "set \\( y=0 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Parallel",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "equal slopes",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Perpendicular",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( m_1m_2=-1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>If \\( f(x)=3x+1 \\), find \\( f(2)-f(0) \\).</p>\\[ 7-1=6. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the x-intercept of \\( 2x+4y=8 \\).</p><p>Set \\( y=0 \\): \\( 2x=8 \\).</p>\\[ x=4. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
